---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party runtime dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unlike the section above, no source from the following is vendored, adapted or
redistributed here; they are ordinary npm dependencies, installed from their
registries under their own licences. They are recorded because this repository's
licence policy admits only Apache-2.0, MIT and BSD, and each of these is inside
it:

    @xyflow/react   MIT   (core/dashboard-ui; React Flow, https://reactflow.dev)

`@xyflow/react` is the renderer behind the `graph` widget type. It is a runtime
dependency of the browser bundle only: `@loams-core/flows`
emits the `nodes`/`edges` pair it mounts and does not import it, which is what
keeps that package testable with no DOM. See
`core/flows/README.md` for why `graph` is a sibling
`Widget.type` rather than a new `ChartSchema.kind`.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream services consumed over HTTP
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The adapters in `packages/plugin-*-adapter/`, together with
`core/bi/`, talk to third-party services as
clients. No source code from any of the following projects is vendored,
redistributed, linked or embedded in this repository; only their HTTP APIs are
called. Because no code from them is shipped, no copyleft obligation is
inherited by this project. This is recorded here for clarity rather than because
any obligation arises:

    ItsAPlan   AGPL-3.0
    Forgejo    GPL-3.0-or-later
    Matomo     GPL-3.0
    OpenPanel  AGPL-3.0
    loams-dev  Apache-2.0

The remaining upstreams (Apache Superset, Zulip, Langfuse, GlitchTip) are
reached the same way, over HTTP only.

Note on naming: `core/bi/` is the client for the BI backend, which speaks the
Apache Superset REST API, so Superset is still the upstream product named above.
The plugin id (`bi`) and the `LOAMS_BI_*` environment variables are this project's
naming; the wire is Superset's.

Note on `loams-dev`: Loams is Apache-2.0, and this adapter calls it exactly as
it calls any other upstream — over HTTP, with no code shared. The proprietary
metering, billing and commercial API surfaces of the Loams platform are not
reachable through, and not used by, this repository.